course: dictionary
lesson: 15278
title: Simplicity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Simplicity is a noun. It means being simple and easy to understand or do, or being plain, with no decoration or extras.
explain: «The teacher explained the sum with great simplicity, so everyone understood it.» The clues are easy to understand and everyone understood, so simplicity means the idea was clear and easy to follow.
explain: «The empty room had white walls and one wooden chair. Its simplicity made it feel calm.» Here simplicity means plain, without decoration. A phrase to remember is «for simplicity», which means to make things easier: «For simplicity, we will use only one colour.»
fact: Simplicity means being simple, plain, or easy to understand or do.
fact: In maths and science, simplicity is valued: a simple rule that explains a lot.
fact: In art and design, simplicity often means plain lines and few colours.
fact: «For simplicity» or «for the sake of simplicity» means to make things easier.
fact: In stories, simplicity can describe a quiet country life, like Mole's simple home in The Wind in the Willows.
exercise: «The simplicity of the rule made it easy to remember.» What does simplicity mean here? | Being a long, hard test | Being costly and fancy | *Being simple and easy to understand | Being very loud and bright
exercise: The room had white walls and one wooden table. What does its simplicity show? | *Being plain, without extras | Lots of decoration | Being full of colours | Being very old
exercise: Find the phrase that means to make things easier. | By accident | *For simplicity | Ask for proof | In the end
test: «Mole lived a life of simplicity in his small home by the river.» What does simplicity mean in this sentence? | *Living plainly and simply | Being lost at sea | Having many visitors | Being rich and busy
test: Which word is closest in meaning to simplicity? | *Plainness | Clutter | Confusion | Complexity
exam: «The scientist wrote the idea down with simplicity, so everyone could follow it.» What does simplicity mean here? | Being loud | Being confusing | Being very expensive | *Being clear and easy to follow
